enzymatic catalysis or extreme conditions) to undergo rearrangement or bond breaking.\n∈=𐑲: As a single amino acid residue, alanine's chemical properties and interactions are confined to its immediate local environment within the peptide chain, without propagating effects across the entire system.\n∋=𐑜: Alanine is one of many interchangeable amino acids that can occupy a specific position in a peptide sequence, meaning any suitable partner from the set of amino acids suffices for that slot.",
